; e = (v2_after - v1_after) / (v1_before - v2_before)
; 
; the single number that spans the entire spectrum of real collisions.
; it is the ratio of relative separation speed to relative approach speed.
; not a force. not an energy. a ratio — dimensionless.
; 
; e = 1  : the collision is perfectly elastic. bodies bounce away at full speed.
; the relative separation speed equals the relative approach speed.
; kinetic energy is fully conserved.
; 
; e = 0  : the collision is perfectly inelastic. bodies stick together.
; the relative separation speed is zero — they move as one.
; maximum kinetic energy is lost (converted to heat, deformation, sound).
; 
; 0 < e < 1 : partial elasticity. real rubber balls, real cars, real baseballs.
; some KE is lost. the bodies separate, but slower than they approached.
; 
; e > 1  : superelastic. explosive separation — energy added by internal mechanism.
; rare. a spring-loaded toy, an explosion between bodies on contact.
; 
; the coefficient of restitution is a material property — it describes the
; interaction between two specific materials, not either body alone.
; it is a property of the sparsha (contact), not of the kshetrajna (individual).
; bounds declare the spectrum

(kosha coefficient-of-restitution
  (vishesa collision-varga)
  (swarupa subanta scalar)
  (siddha dimensionless)
  (yukta velocity material)
  (abheda ratio sparsha)
  (drishthanta elastic-collision inelastic-collision))
